Notes


.high-level Python web framework for building secure, scalable backend frameworks fast 
.handles the backend of a web app:
            .routing - URLs > functions
            .DB models - ORM 
            .authentication
            .admin dashboard
            .security
            .templates - HTML rendering
            .middleware
            .forms
            .sessions
            .caching 

.core philosophy 
    ."batteries-included" - no need to install packages 
    .DRY principle - write logic once, reuse everywhere 
    .convention over configuration - gives a standard structure so that the project stays clean and predictable 

.django project structure 
    .myproject/
        manage.py - commandline tools for migraitions, running server, creating apps 
        myproject/
            settings.py   - project's brain; DB, apps, middleware, security
            urls.py  - routing table 
            asgi/wsgi.py   -  deployment entry points 

.django's MVT architecture 
    .model - DB layer; tables represented as Python classes 
    .view - business logic; what happens when a request hits the server 
    .template - HTML rendering; what the user sees 
    
    .it gives the flow:  user > url > view > model > template > response 

.django's ORM
    .write Python classes instead of writing SQL manually 
    

.django's admin 
    .gives full admin dashboard instantly 
    .no coding required 

.django migrations 
    .version control for my DB schema 
    .use migrations to generate SQL when changing a model 


.django security
    .protects automatically from:
        .SQL injection
        .clickjacking
        .session hijacking 


.django use cases 
    .good for:
        .hospitals/inventory/CRMs/dashboards/APIs/authentication systems/admin-heavy apps

    






Project fundamentals 
.creating a project
    .root of everything 
        .manage.py - command center
        .settings.py - configuration brain
        .urls.py - routing map
        .wsgi.py/asgi.py - deployment entry points 


.understanding the setting file 
    .django becomes a framework and not a script 
    .understand:
        .installed_apps
        .middleware
        .templates
        .databases
        .static_url/media_url
        .auth_user_model 

    .all django workings are controlled here 

.creating my first app
    .a django project is a container
    .an app is a functional module inside it 
        .runs in the outer project directory:
            .manage.py is what registers and manages apps
            .djangp expects apps to be siblings of the inner project folder 
            .keeps the project clean and modular 
        
